{
  "id": "ss.relic.firstbite",
  "name": "First bite",
  "description": "A pale egg of a body with one clean bite out of its upper right — the silhouette carries the scoop, and the scoop's edge is scalloped by a row of six teeth. The wound is lit, not dark: the flesh the bite exposes is a wide band of white following the curve, paler than the skin around it and rimmed with a thin dark line where skin becomes flesh, because a dark cavity ringed in pale skin is an eye or a hole whatever it was meant to be, and this relic is about a bite landing, not a body losing something. The first hit on any body lands double, so the one image is a first bite, complete, with nothing else on the plate. Deliberately not a fruit with a stalk (the plate already has a cap, a flask and a jar for containers) and not the egg from ss.relic.shrink, which is grey, upright and mostly hollow: this one is warm, tilted and solid. An earlier pass shaded the whole lower half dark and got a moon.",
